## Usage Examples

```javascript
import { clamp, lerp, randomInt } from './mathUtils.js';

// --- clamp ---
console.log(clamp(15,  0, 10));  // 10  (above max → capped)
console.log(clamp(-5,  0, 10));  // 0   (below min → capped)
console.log(clamp( 7,  0, 10));  // 7   (within range → unchanged)

// --- lerp ---
console.log(lerp(0, 200, 0));    // 0
console.log(lerp(0, 200, 0.25)); // 50
console.log(lerp(0, 200, 0.5));  // 100
console.log(lerp(0, 200, 1));    // 200

// --- randomInt ---
const roll = randomInt(1, 6);
console.log(roll);               // 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6

// Combine them: random value clamped to a range
const raw = lerp(-50, 150, Math.random()); // −50 … 150
const safe = clamp(raw, 0, 100);           // 0 … 100
console.log(safe);
```

---

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| Named exports | Allows consumers to import only what they need and enables tree-shaking |
| `min > max` guard | Catches swapped arguments early with a descriptive error |
| `lerp` allows `t` outside `[0, 1]` | Extrapolation is a legitimate use-case; callers can wrap with `clamp` if needed |
| `Math.floor(random * (max - min + 1)) + min` | Standard unbiased formula for inclusive integer ranges |

