## How it works

### `stripAccents(str)`

| Step | What happens | Example |
|------|-------------|---------|
| `.normalize('NFD')` | Decomposes precomposed characters into a base letter + one or more combining marks | `'é'` → `'e\u0301'` |
| `.replace(/\p{Mn}/gu, '')` | Removes every **Unicode non-spacing mark** (the combining diacritics) | `'e\u0301'` → `'e'` |

The `\p{Mn}` Unicode property escape requires the `u` flag and is supported in all modern JS engines (Node ≥ 10, V8 ≥ 6.3).

### `slugify(str)`

| Step | Regex / method | Purpose |
|------|---------------|---------|
| 1 | `.trim()` | Remove surrounding whitespace |
| 2 | `stripAccents` per character | `'é'` → `'e'`, `'ü'` → `'u'` |
| 3 | `.toLowerCase()` | Uniform casing |
| 4 | `/&/g` → `' and '` | Preserve meaning of ampersands |
| 5 | `/[^a-z0-9\s-]/g` | Drop punctuation, symbols, etc. |
| 6 | `/[\s-]+/g` → `'-'` | Collapse gaps into single hyphens |
| 7 | `/^-+\|-+$/g` | Clean up edge hyphens |

