## Key Design Decisions

| Concern | Choice |
|---|---|
| **Regex parsing** | Single regex captures all optional groups; avoids `Date.parse()` whose behaviour is implementation-defined for non-UTC strings |
| **Offset handling** | Offsets are subtracted when parsing (local → UTC) and added when formatting (UTC → local wall-clock) |
| **Millisecond normalisation** | Sub-second digits are left-padded to 3 digits so `"1"` → 100 ms, not 1 ms |
| **Calendar validation** | Uses `Date.UTC(year, month, 0)` to find the real last day of any month (handles leap years automatically) |
| **No external dependencies** | Pure stdlib — works in Node.js and modern browsers |

